1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,600
Good morning, Synmouth Museum. Can I help you?

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:07,783
Oh yes. Good morning. I'm interested in the children's workshops

3
00:00:07,783 --> 00:00:11,130
and I'd like a little more information, please.

4
00:00:11,130 --> 00:00:13,740
Do you mean the Art and Craft workshops?

5
00:00:13,740 --> 00:00:16,400
Yes. A friend of a friend mentioned them

6
00:00:16,660 --> 00:00:19,510
The children do painting and make models and so forth.

7
00:00:19,510 --> 00:00:23,820
Yes, of course. Um, where to begin

8
00:00:24,680 --> 00:00:28,640
First of all, as you probably know, they run every Saturday.

9
00:00:28,640 --> 00:00:31,670
Fine. And what about ages?

10
00:00:31,670 --> 00:00:34,553
Well, all ages from five upwards are welcome,

11
00:00:34,553 --> 00:00:40,320
though we do ask that children below eight years of age are accompanied by an adult.

12
00:00:40,320 --> 00:00:44,430
Fine. That wouldn't be a problem. What about cost?

13
00:00:44,430 --> 00:00:47,559
Well, I think you'll find them very reasonable.

14
00:00:47,559 --> 00:00:54,600
It's £2.50 a child, with 80 pence off for two or more children from the same family.

15
00:00:54,600 --> 00:00:59,580
Oh yes, very reasonable. And are they held in the main museum?

16
00:00:59,580 --> 00:01:02,460
Not exactly. They're nearby.

17
00:01:02,460 --> 00:01:07,140
Could you give me the full address? I don't know the area very well.

18
00:01:07,140 --> 00:01:10,540
Yes, it's Winter House.

19
00:01:10,540 --> 00:01:11,790
Right.

20
00:01:11,790 --> 00:01:15,360
And that's in Tamer Street.

21
00:01:15,360 --> 00:01:17,530
Could you spell that please?

22
00:01:17,530 --> 00:01:23,620
Yes, T-A-M-E-R Street.

23
00:01:23,620 --> 00:01:24,960
Lovely.

24
00:01:24,960 --> 00:01:29,126
And I do need to tell you that there's a security entrance,

25
00:01:29,126 --> 00:01:33,987
so you need to press the green button for someone to let you in.

26
00:01:33,987 --> 00:01:38,500
Don't press the red button please, but don't worry, it's all clearly labelled.

27
00:01:38,500 --> 00:01:43,460
OK. And one more question. Is parking available nearby

28
00:01:43,900 --> 00:01:45,790
We're driving in from out of town.

29
00:01:45,790 --> 00:01:53,687
Your best bet is to leave your car at the back of the library-on a Saturday morning there are plenty of spaces there.

30
00:01:53,687 --> 00:01:56,090
It's right next door to the museum.

31
00:01:56,090 --> 00:01:59,650
And can I ask about booking places?

32
00:01:59,650 --> 00:02:02,720
Yes, and I must tell you

33
00:02:02,920 --> 00:02:06,370
you really should book by calling the education department here.

34
00:02:06,370 --> 00:02:11,900
Oh, I'm sorry, should I have rung them instead of the main museum number?

35
00:02:11,900 --> 00:02:15,835
No, that's fine this time, please don't worry.

36
00:02:15,835 --> 00:02:22,230
But for future reference, I'll give you the direct number. It's two hundred-seven-six-five.

37
00:02:22,230 --> 00:02:24,420
Great, I've got that.

38
00:02:24,420 --> 00:02:31,590
But I'm very happy to give you information about the next two workshops.

39
00:02:31,590 --> 00:02:35,450
On Saturday the 16th there's Building Castles.

40
00:02:35,450 --> 00:02:37,330
Oh, sounds great!

41
00:02:37,330 --> 00:02:43,000
This involves quite a bit of glue, so just make sure the kids are in old clothes.

42
00:02:43,000 --> 00:02:45,940
I know, ones I don't mind getting mucky.

43
00:02:45,940 --> 00:02:49,620
Exactly. And if possible, could you bring along bottle tops

44
00:02:49,620 --> 00:02:55,140
which the children might be able to use in the models, you know, as decoration?

45
00:02:55,140 --> 00:02:57,730
We'll certainly try to find some for you.

46
00:02:57,730 --> 00:03:00,110
Then the following week...

47
00:03:00,110 --> 00:03:02,740
That'll be the 23rd, won't it?

48
00:03:02,740 --> 00:03:07,852
Yes, that's right. On that day, it's what we call Undersea Worlds.

49
00:03:07,852 --> 00:03:13,390
This is where they make scenes with fishes, underground caverns and so on.

50
00:03:13,390 --> 00:03:17,830
IS that likely to get very dirty? Lots of paint splashes?

51
00:03:17,830 --> 00:03:21,852
Not really, so we don't recommend any special clothes for that one.

52
00:03:21,852 --> 00:03:27,549
But if you could search out some silver paper to bring along to use in the sessions,

53
00:03:27,549 --> 00:03:30,900
you know, it's shiny. It looks like water, that'd be great.

54
00:03:30,900 --> 00:03:34,400
Yes, of course. We'll see what we can come up with

55
00:03:34,780 --> 00:03:37,740
Well, thank you ever so much for all your help.

56
00:03:37,740 --> 00:03:42,300
The sessions sound really good and I'll certainly book up for the next two.

57
00:03:42,300 --> 00:03:45,440
Lovely. Thanks very much for ringing.

58
00:03:45,440 --> 00:03:46,410
Bye.

59
00:03:46,410 --> 00:03:47,560
Bye-bye.
